{
  "name": "STRIX - Approved Content to Facebook (v2)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STRIX Auto-Publish Workflow (v2)\n\n1. Reads the STRIX Content Queue sheet\n2. Keeps only rows where Status = Approved\n3. For each: finds the image in Drive, downloads it, uploads it to the public GitHub repo, waits for it to propagate, builds its public URL, posts it to the Facebook Page, then marks the row Posted\n\nYou approve rows manually in the Google Sheet (Draft -> Approved) - nothing here posts anything you haven't reviewed.\n\nNOTE: the \"Upload to GitHub\" node has not been live-tested yet (everything from \"Find Image File\" onward through Facebook HAS been tested and confirmed working today, using an image already sitting in GitHub). If the GitHub upload step errors, the most likely fix is the binary-to-base64 expression on that node - flag it and we'll debug it together.",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 420
      },
      "id": "note-overview",
      "name": "Read Me",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-220, -80]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "cronExpression",
              "expression": "0 9 * * *"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "trigger-schedule",
      "name": "Daily Check (9am)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [240, 260]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
